# No agent attribution in git

When creating commits, pull requests, or any pushed content for this repository:

- **Never** add `Co-authored-by:` trailers naming Cursor, cursorAgent, Composer, or any AI tool.
- **Never** mention Cursor, cursorAgent, or an AI agent name in commit messages, PR titles, PR bodies, or code comments added for this project.
- Commit messages describe **project changes only** — what changed and why, in neutral technical language.

## Commits

```text
# Bad
Fix workflow

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# Good
Fix GHCR publish workflow frontend build in CI.
```

## Pull requests

Same rule: no tool or agent branding in title or body.

## If attribution is added automatically

Some environments append `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` on commit. **Remove it before push** — amend the message or rewrite the commit so it never reaches the remote.
